      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Since 1559, the Archbishop of Mechelen has been the primate of all Low Countries, a role formalized that year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archdiocese_of_Mechelen%E2%80%93Brussels",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mechelen hosts Rumbold's Cathedral, while Brussels shares the archdiocese’s seat with St. Peter's Cathedral.",
